1
00:00:05,428 --> 00:00:07,870
Whiskers and the Rainbow's End.

2
00:00:16,421 --> 00:00:20,193
It had rained all week, and the pond was brimming over.

3
00:00:20,393 --> 00:00:24,205
Rain, rain, rain. Even my naps are getting soggy.

4
00:00:28,162 --> 00:00:31,065
Whiskers, look! Something shiny is floating in the pond!

5
00:00:31,265 --> 00:00:34,187
A shiny glass fish! Leave this to me.

6
00:00:42,737 --> 00:00:45,158
Got it! Hmm. A very crunchy fish.

7
00:00:48,699 --> 00:00:52,390
A map of Ireland! Follow the rainbow, to the treasure at its end.

8
00:00:52,590 --> 00:00:55,346
In the old stories, a pot of gold waits there.

9
00:00:55,546 --> 00:00:59,415
A pot of goldfish? Luna, why are we still standing here?

10
00:01:02,538 --> 00:01:07,487
So the cats sailed across the Irish Sea, on a big green ferry to Dublin.

11
00:01:16,037 --> 00:01:18,904
Is the sea supposed to go up and down this much?

12
00:01:19,104 --> 00:01:20,563
Look, Whiskers! Dublin!

13
00:01:30,783 --> 00:01:34,662
Dublin was full of doors, in every colour of the rainbow.

14
00:01:34,862 --> 00:01:38,332
The map says: begin at the bridge that once cost half a penny.

15
00:01:45,212 --> 00:01:48,628
That's the Ha'penny Bridge, little cats, over the River Liffey!

16
00:01:48,828 --> 00:01:52,073
We haven't got a penny. We haven't even got half.

17
00:01:52,273 --> 00:01:57,145
Ha! It's free now. I'm Fergal. That map leads west, to the Cliffs of Moher. I'll take you!

18
00:02:05,278 --> 00:02:10,006
In a cosy pub, fiddles and tin whistles played jigs and reels.

19
00:02:16,051 --> 00:02:18,709
Is that bread? Warm bread? With butter?

20
00:02:18,909 --> 00:02:21,733
Soda bread, fresh from the oven. Help yourself!

21
00:02:27,778 --> 00:02:30,248
Come on, Whiskers! Everybody's dancing!

22
00:02:41,303 --> 00:02:44,657
I did that on purpose. It's a very advanced step.

23
00:02:49,868 --> 00:02:55,094
Next morning, Fergal's painted caravan rolled west over the green hills.

24
00:03:02,809 --> 00:03:06,454
See that round tower? Long ago, monks kept their books safe up there.

25
00:03:10,412 --> 00:03:13,365
More rain? This country is one big puddle!

26
00:03:13,565 --> 00:03:15,795
Ah, but no rain, no rainbows.

27
00:03:23,511 --> 00:03:25,800
There it is! And look, it ends at the cliffs!

28
00:03:28,923 --> 00:03:32,444
Ooh, a four-leaf clover. That's lucky. I'm keeping it.

29
00:03:40,994 --> 00:03:45,434
At last, the Cliffs of Moher, high above the wild Atlantic.

30
00:03:45,634 --> 00:03:47,957
The rainbow ends right there, on that ledge!

31
00:03:48,157 --> 00:03:50,011
My goldfish! Here I come!

32
00:03:53,551 --> 00:03:56,019
Help! Please! My little lamb Dot is stuck!

33
00:04:00,394 --> 00:04:03,312
Whiskers, the rainbow's fading! We'll lose the treasure!

34
00:04:07,270 --> 00:04:10,730
Forget the treasure. Hold on, little one! I'm coming!

35
00:04:23,456 --> 00:04:25,844
Dot! Oh, thank you, thank you, brave cats!

36
00:04:26,044 --> 00:04:29,404
Here, little one. A lucky clover, just for you.

37
00:04:35,449 --> 00:04:37,900
Oh. The rainbow's gone. No treasure.

38
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:41,832
That rainbow ended right where somebody needed you. That's real luck.

39
00:04:42,032 --> 00:04:45,546
Come home with me. I've a pot of something golden on the stove.

40
00:04:53,262 --> 00:04:57,148
A pot of gold! Golden fish chowder! The legend was true!

41
00:05:03,193 --> 00:05:05,477
You gave away your lucky clover, Whiskers.

42
00:05:05,677 --> 00:05:08,985
I know. And somehow, I feel luckier than ever.

43
00:05:18,371 --> 00:05:22,871
Back home, the rain had stopped, and a rainbow shone over the garden.

44
00:05:23,071 --> 00:05:25,075
So? Did you find the pot of gold?

45
00:05:25,275 --> 00:05:28,265
Better, Pip. We found out what luck is for.

46
00:05:28,465 --> 00:05:31,863
Let's send our own map. Someone else might follow a rainbow too.

47
00:05:39,578 --> 00:05:43,944
Because luck isn't something you keep. It's something you give away.

